# {{title}} {#b-top}

Every line below is part of a tree an agent can address. Prose is a *flow*
paragraph, so it carries inline markup — **strong**, ~~struck~~, `inline code`,
math $a^2 + b^2$, a [link](https://geml-spec.github.io/geml/) — and it can point
at any block by id: see [[#b-facts]] and the note at [[#b-checked]].[^b-why]

Values from `meta` interpolate: this is chapter {{chapter}}, against GEML
{{spec}}. Change `title` above and the heading follows.

=== note {.tip #b-note}
A `note` is a callout, not a paragraph with a class glued on — it is a typed
block, so an agent can find every callout in a corpus with one query. Intent
goes on a class: `{.tip}`, `{.warning}`, `{.aside}`.
===

