## A block has an id, and an id is a contract {#b-facts}

=== table {#b-revenue caption="Revenue by segment" format=csv header=1}
Segment, Q1, Q2
Cloud,    8, 10
Platform, 5,  6
===

That table is *facts only*. Nothing is derived here — deriving is what the next
chapter is about.

=== note {#b-checked .warning}
Every reference is checked when the document is parsed: `[[#id]]`, a link to
`#id`, a footnote, a chart's `data=#id`. Press **Break a reference** above and
watch the pill flip red — nothing renders a dangling pointer quietly.
===

%% A %% line is a comment. It stays in the model and never reaches the page.

=== note {#b-why}
Markdown has no ids, so an agent must re-read the whole file to change one
paragraph. GEML gives every block an address, and `geml set <file> '#id'`
rewrites exactly that block — the footnote you just followed is itself a block.
===
